From: Tai Ci maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Fail compilation when a child function has no constant slot

cpool_add() returns -1 when growing the constant pool fails, but its callers
store that as the child function's parent_cpool_idx and keep parsing. After
a single transient allocation failure the parse can still succeed, and
js_create_function() then hits assert(cpool_idx >= 0) (abort; an
out-of-bounds store with NDEBUG). It now frees the child function object,
reports out of memory and takes its existing failure path.

Upstream quickjs-ng df836d1 contains the defect.
Found by the one-failure mode of Tai's runtime.js compile sweep
(tests/test_quickjs_oom.c).
---
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -37000,8 +37000,13 @@
         func_obj = js_create_function(ctx, fd1);
         if (JS_IsException(func_obj))
             goto fail;
+        /* cpool_add() fails without stopping the parser, leaving -1 */
+        if (cpool_idx < 0) {
+            JS_FreeValue(ctx, func_obj);
+            JS_ThrowOutOfMemory(ctx);
+            goto fail;
+        }
         /* save it in the constant pool */
-        assert(cpool_idx >= 0);
         fd->cpool[cpool_idx] = func_obj;
     }
 
